//? Title: Pancake sort: actual prefix reversals
//? Subtitle: Canonical C++ producers, original fixtures and explicit controls
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
The greedy producer finds the first maximum of each unsorted prefix, brings it
to the top if necessary, then reverses the prefix to settle it. Already-settled
maxima cause no reversal. For n>=1 there are at most2(n-1) flips, with quadratic
worst-case comparisons and element movement. This is not a shortest-flip solver
and is not stable. Integer fixtures isolate the mechanism; no dataset is needed.
)

\toc

> Mechanism and scope

The greedy producer finds the first maximum of each unsorted prefix, brings it
to the top if necessary, then reverses the prefix to settle it. Already-settled
maxima cause no reversal. For n>=1 there are at most2(n-1) flips, with quadratic
worst-case comparisons and element movement. This is not a shortest-flip solver
and is not stable. Integer fixtures isolate the mechanism; no dataset is needed.

$$ P_k(a)_i = a_{k-1-i}\ (i<k),\qquad P_k(a)_i=a_i\ (i\ge k). $$

> A tiny actual producing history

The table and native diagram use the same producing run. Captured records own
their values; the report does not reconstruct the algorithm.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/pancake_sort_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto t = dm::algorithms::pancake_sort_trace({3, 1, 2});
    std::print("| prefix | first maximum index | comparisons | actual post-state |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | " "--- |\n");
    for (auto &r : t.steps)
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | `{}` |\n", r.prefix, r.maximum_index,
                   r.comparisons, r.values);
    dm::graphics::Diagram d;
    d.node("n0", {0, 0},
           std::format("Initial actual state\n{}", t.states.front()));
    d.node("n1", {8, 0},
           std::format("Actual reversal lengths\n{}", t.result.flips));
    d.node("n2", {16, 0}, std::format("Final actual state\n{}", t.result.sorted));
    d.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    d.save_svg("build/pancake_sort_tiny.svg");
}
```
